Something weird that I noticed was that the config entry for the P110 had these conn params:
```
          "connection_params": {
            "connection_parameters": {
              "tplink_device_type": "Unknown",
              "encryption_type": "XOR"
            }
          }
```
Same for the bulb. Strangely enough, both of the devices can be controlled just fine after a homeassistant restart.. :-)

I can see my username and pw (in cleartext, but I suppose that's how it is) in `$HOMEASSISTANT_HOME/.storage/tplink`.Changing the pw there will cause a never-ending loop with `Error connecting to device 192.168.xx, trying discovery: Unable to connect to the device: 192.168.xx: 'result'` without indication to reconfigure the device.

Seeing also `-1501` and `9999` error codes coming in for the handshake:
```
[kasa.aestransport] Handshake with 192.168.xx complete
[kasa.aestransport] secure_passthrough response is 200: {'error_code': 0, 'result': {'response': 'xxx'}}
[kasa.aestransport] decrypted secure_passthrough response is {"error_code":-1501}
[kasa.aestransport] secure_passthrough response is 200: {'error_code': 9999}
[kasa.aestransport] Will perform handshaking..
[kasa.aestransport] Generating keypair
```
